<!--
  Sitemap for https://gymflow.sbs

  ONE URL, and that is correct. `react-router-dom` is listed in package.json but
  no router is ever mounted: src/main.tsx renders <App /> directly, and App.tsx is
  a single scrolling page (Hero, Features, WhatsApp, HowItWorks, InteractiveDemo,
  Mobile, Pricing, Testimonials, Footer). The nav links are in-page anchors such
  as #features and #pricing.

  Anchors are deliberately NOT listed. A fragment is not a separate URL — Google
  resolves #pricing to this same page, so listing them adds nothing and can look
  like keyword padding. If a section is ever promoted to a real route (for example
  /pricing served as its own HTML entry in vite.config.ts), add it here then.

  `changefreq` and `priority` are omitted on purpose: Google ignores both. Only
  <loc> and <lastmod> carry weight, and lastmod only while it stays honest — bump
  it when the page content changes meaningfully, or it will simply be disregarded.
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url>
    <loc>https://gymflow.sbs/</loc>
    <lastmod>2026-09-03</lastmod>
  </url>
</urlset>
